iven-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecularstraintyping of Mycobacteriumtuberculosis to confirm cross-contamination in themycobacteriologylaboratory and modification of procedures to minimize occurrence of falsepositivecultures</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Clinical Microbiology</italic></source><year>1993</year><volume>31</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>1677</fpage><lpage>1682</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8102372</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Egol</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jazrawi</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>DeWal</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Su</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Leslie</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Cesare</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Orthopaedic manifestations of systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source><italic>Bulletin: Hospital for Joint Diseases</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>60</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>34</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loehrl</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inflammatory and granulomatous lesions of the larynx and pharynx</article-title><source><italic>American Journal of Medicine</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>111</volume><issue>8</issue></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karim</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Siddiqui</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Marder</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattana</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Severeupperairwayobstruction fromcricoarytenoiditis as the sole presenting manifestation of a systemic lupuserythematosusflare</article-title><source><italic>Chest</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>121</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>990</fpage><lpage>993</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11888989</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doria</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Briani</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lupus: improving long-term prognosis</article-title><source><italic>Lupus</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>17</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>166</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18372355</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Nasofibroscopic view of the larynx in maximum abduction showing left vocal cord immobility in adduction.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CRIM.RHEUMATOLOGY2011-317379.001"/></fig></floats-group></article>